# Safe editing behavior

When working in this repository, follow these editing rules:

- Do not rewrite large sections of the app unless explicitly requested
- Make the smallest effective change that solves the problem
- Preserve existing working animations, structure, and styling unless the task requires changing them
- Do not rename files, components, routes, or imports unless necessary
- Do not remove GSAP, Locomotive Scroll, or other motion logic unless there is a confirmed issue
- Before editing, inspect related files and understand how the section is connected
- If a change may affect multiple sections, explain the impact first
- Prefer targeted refactors over broad rewrites
- Do not replace existing sections with completely new versions unless explicitly requested
- Use the current implementation as the starting point and improve it incrementally
- Preserve the current design intent whenever possible
- Do not make unnecessary visual or structural changes just because another approach is possible
- Avoid introducing placeholder content unless explicitly requested
- Keep code readable and production-oriented
- When fixing or building a section, do not validate it at only one screen size. Check its behavior across the full responsive range before considering the change complete (see `responsive-mobile-first.mdc`).

See also `preserve-existing-work.mdc`.
